ios: stay logged in (no IDLE_TIMER)

After 90 s without input the client sends IDLE_TIMER (the server may then log the player out) and
arms logoutTimer=250, which turns any connection hiccup in the next 5 s into a logout. With
lcHost.settings.stayLoggedIn (read live) the client does neither; everything else is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/client/Client.ts b/src/client/Client.ts
index 04a5550..3d40b37 100644
--- a/src/client/Client.ts
+++ b/src/client/Client.ts
@@ -2366,7 +2366,9 @@ export class Client extends GameShell {
 
         await this.handleInputKey();
 
-        if (now - this.idleTimer > 90_000) {
+        // custom (ios): single-player "stay logged in" (lcHost.settings.stayLoggedIn): never report idling, so the
+        // server is not asked to log the player out and no logout countdown turns a later hiccup into a logout
+        if (now - this.idleTimer > 90_000 && !lcSetting('stayLoggedIn', false)) {
             // no input in 90s, notify the server
             this.logoutTimer = 250;
             this.idleTimer += 10_000; // 10s backoff
